{"title":"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> real, the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51dd46be3987d84255141b6925ceaac8a7789847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le |x-2|\\le 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> is equivalent to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d7e50eefbf141ad5f3e11472fe2ffaf4193f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }x\\le 1\\text{ or }x\\ge 3\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1\\le x\\le 3\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }-5\\le x\\le 9\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D) }-5\\le x\\le 1\\text{ or }3\\le x\\le 9\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }-6\\le x\\le 1\\text{ or }3\\le x\\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"515\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the inequality into two smaller inequalities and solve them individually.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b7271f85aa009141ce0d6c1585df81f6cc9e81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x-2| \\ge 1 \\quad \\rightarrow \\quad x \\ge 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x \\le 1\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24383626db3f8ce407696f33910d8b3dda7a88f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x-2| \\le 7 \\quad \\rightarrow \\quad x \\le 9 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x \\ge -5\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Combining these inequalities, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/6371f16354eb80207efbe1b8573faad6820d0643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [-5, 1] \\cup [3, 9].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4feb78447beef6c93631b0912fb24e7936b6dad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>-edited by coolmath34\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017143911\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 32/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1571/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20482:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017143911 and revision id 271816. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}